    <GaugingStation location="Mouth Bridge" name="Blackadder Water" number="21027">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station on the Blackadder Water.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Moderate seasonal weed growth effects rating. Peak flow ratings derived from current meter gaugings up to 2.4m (about 2 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station. Natural river section, about 13m wide, with rock control.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural flow regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Natural catchment. Mostly Old Red Sandstone and calciferous sandstone overlain by Boulder Clay. Grazing on hills, arable on lower land; some forest. No significant catchment changes known.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="No comment." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Nearly all flows are contained and the ratings are informed by a flood gauging at 2.357m , measured at 85.7 cumecs." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
